DESCRIPTION >
    Usage for one meter, optionally one subject, over a half-open window of event
    time. The question an invoice is derived from.

    The window is `[date_from, date_to)`: `date_from` inclusive, `date_to`
    exclusive, so consecutive periods tile without the event on the boundary
    being counted in both. Both are ISO 8601 instants; a string carrying no
    offset is read as UTC rather than as the server's zone.

    `total` and `event_count` come back as strings. A quantity is an Int64 and a
    sum of them can pass 2^53, where a JSON number stops being able to represent
    every integer. The caller parses the string and refuses a total it cannot
    hold exactly, which is a visible failure rather than a silently rounded
    invoice.

TOKEN "medusa_usage" READ

NODE collapse
DESCRIPTION >
    One row per event key, before anything is summed.

    This is what makes "at most one row per key" true the moment a duplicate is
    written rather than whenever a background merge runs. `argMax(..., version)`
    picks the earliest-ingested copy, the same copy `ReplacingMergeTree` keeps,
    so the answer here does not change when a merge collapses the rows on disk.

    The window filter is applied before the collapse so the read stays on the
    sorting key's prefix. The only case where that differs from collapsing first
    is a key whose copies carry different `occurred_at` values that straddle a
    period boundary, which requires a caller to have reused an explicit
    idempotency key across events with different facts.
SQL >
    %
    SELECT
        key,
        argMax(quantity, version) AS event_quantity,
        argMax(occurred_at, version) AS event_occurred_at
    FROM usage_events
    WHERE
        meter = {{String(meter, required=True, description='The meter to aggregate, compared byte for byte.')}}
        AND occurred_at >= parseDateTime64BestEffort({{String(date_from, '1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z', required=True, description='Inclusive lower bound on event time, ISO 8601.')}}, 3, 'UTC')
        AND occurred_at < parseDateTime64BestEffort({{String(date_to, '1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z', required=True, description='Exclusive upper bound on event time, ISO 8601.')}}, 3, 'UTC')
        {% if defined(subject) %}
        AND subject = {{String(subject, description='Restrict to one subject. Omitted, every subject on the meter is aggregated.')}}
        {% end %}
        {% if defined(property_keys) %}
        AND arrayAll(
            i ->
                JSONHas(properties, {{Array(property_keys, 'String', description='Dimension names to filter on, positionally paired with property_values.')}}[i])
                AND JSONExtractRaw(properties, {{Array(property_keys, 'String')}}[i]) = {{Array(property_values, 'String', description='Canonical JSON of each dimension value: strings quoted, numbers bare.')}}[i],
            range(1, length({{Array(property_keys, 'String')}}) + 1)
        )
        {% end %}
    GROUP BY key

NODE endpoint
SQL >
    SELECT
        toString(sum(event_quantity)) AS total,
        toString(count()) AS event_count,
        toUnixTimestamp64Milli(minOrNull(event_occurred_at)) AS first_occurred_at,
        toUnixTimestamp64Milli(maxOrNull(event_occurred_at)) AS last_occurred_at
    FROM collapse

TYPE ENDPOINT
